# scope.env — optional per-machine launcher settings.
#
# Copy to `scope.env` (git-ignored) and edit. Read by apps/scope-desktop/scope-control.js
# when the app boots from the desktop icon, which inherits no shell environment.
# Real environment variables always win, so `SCOPE_HOST=0.0.0.0 ./run.sh` still
# overrides whatever is set here. Plain KEY=VALUE lines; `#` comments allowed.

# ── Reach Pi Scope from a phone on the same Wi-Fi ────────────────────────────
# Default is 127.0.0.1 (this machine only). Set 0.0.0.0 to also bind every
# interface, which is what makes the header's phone button show a scannable QR.
#
# Only do this on a network you trust. With this set, anything on the LAN that
# knows the token gets the full UI — including the Terminal view, which is a
# real shell on this host. The token is minted randomly at boot and written to
# tmp/scope_token (mode 0600); the QR in the app carries it.
# SCOPE_HOST=0.0.0.0

# ── Pin the auth token (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# By default a random token is minted per run. Uncomment to keep the phone URL
# stable across restarts (e.g. if you bookmarked it). Generate a good one with:
#   openssl rand -hex 24
# SCOPE_AUTH_TOKEN=

# ── Change the port (optional, default 43190) ───────────────────────────────
# SCOPE_PORT=43190
